<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=fax">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Communication and computing</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fax</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1843">1843</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Facsimile, Telefax, Telecopying</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fax, short for facsimile, is the transmission of scanned printed text and images by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telephone">telephone</a> to a printer at the other end. The Scottish inventor Alexander Bain received British patent 9745 on 27 May 1843 for his Electric <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">Printing</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Telegraph</a> and reproduced graphic signs in laboratory experiments in 1846. Giovanni Caselli's Pantelegraph began the first commercial telefax service between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> in 1865, some 11 years before the telephone. Arthur Korn's Bildtelegraph sent a wanted-person photograph from Paris to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1908. Fax machines became common in offices in the 1980s and 1990s and were later largely replaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/email">email</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fax.jpg" alt="Fax" width="330" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pittigrilli; derivative work by Georgfotoart · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panasonic_KX-F90_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1843</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>United Kingdom</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Alexander Bain · Giovanni Caselli · <a href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Bain's patent is given as 1843 but his laboratory reproduction of graphic signs to 1846; the first commercial service, Caselli's, began in 1865.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Electrical telegraph<span>1816</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=fax">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
